cat > requirements.txt << 'EOF'
numpy
scipy
pillow
torch
torchvision
transformers
scikit-learn
matplotlib
EOF

cat > README.md << 'EOF'
# When do a few labeled examples improve on CLIP zero-shot classification?

CLIP ViT-B/32 zero-shot vs. a logistic-regression probe on frozen CLIP features,
on a 20-class subset of Oxford Flowers 102.

## Data
Download from https://www.robots.ox.ac.uk/~vgg/data/flowers/102/ :
`102flowers.tgz` (extract to `jpg/`), `imagelabels.mat`, `setid.mat`.

## Run
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    python make_subset.py        # builds flowers20/ (seed 42)
    python extract_features.py   # CLIP features -> features.npz
    python zero_shot.py          # zero-shot baseline
    python few_shot.py           # probe at k = 1, 2, 4, 8, 10 -> results.csv, accuracy_vs_k.png

## Environment
Python 3.10, PyTorch, Transformers, scikit-learn (CPU).
EOF